  "notes": "FORMS:\nCompound verb: {動|うご}く (to move) + {出|だ}す (to begin). The ～{出|だ}す pattern indicates the beginning of an action: {歩|ある}き{出|だ}す (to start walking), {泣|な}き{出|だ}す (to start crying), {降|ふ}り{出|だ}す (to start raining).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ゆっくり{動|うご}き{出|だ}す (to start moving slowly)\n- いよいよ{動|うご}き{出|だ}す (to finally get going)\n- {一斉|いっせい}に{動|うご}き{出|だ}す (to all start moving at once)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {動|うご}き{始|はじ}める: to begin to move — synonymous, slightly more formal\n- {始動|しどう}する: to start up — technical, for machines and engines\n- {発進|はっしん}する: to depart, to set off — for vehicles",
